  "prefLabel": "Rev 1108.09 Object Code 900: Other Uses of Funds",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Rev 1108.09 Object Code 900: Other Uses of Funds.\n\n(a) Object code 900, other uses of funds classification, shall be used to classify transactions which are not properly recorded as expenditures to the LEA, but require budgetary or accounting control.\n\n(b) Object code 910, fund transfers out, classification shall be used for all transactions conveying money from one fund to another without recourse.\n\nSource. #6869, eff 10-20-98; ss by #8306, eff 3-22-05; ss by #10304, eff 3-22-13; ss by #13503, eff 12-9-22",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/rev1100.html"
